# Fictional EP Tracklist

## Track 1: Clap Comes After the Ticket Punch

**Story & Context:** At 104 BPM, Marcus opens with a compact swingbeat pattern built from short kick, rimshot, close clap, and swung hats. Emi enters with one hard sanshin strike a swung sixteenth before every second clap. The first Skin Pickup is low tonic; the second is a muted rake; the third begins a semitone slide that locks to the snare. Maya plays soft minor-7 FM chords and leaves the final eighth of each bar empty. Riku’s synth bass answers only after Emi’s low-string attacks rather than doubling them. In the chorus, one programmed clap disappears completely and Clap Shadow replaces it with a dry snakeskin-backed rake.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Close-up of an old ferry ticket punch beside a lacquered sanshin body, one red fare stamp slightly misaligned on cream paper, rain on terminal glass, green desk-lamp reflection. Sparse lyric fragments: “ticket punch,” “clap comes after,” “one step early,” “まだ閉めない / don’t close it yet.”

## Track 2: Three Strings Under Window Six

**Story & Context:** At 112 BPM, the EP’s most kinetic track uses Three-String Relay explicitly. Low string owns tonic pickups, middle string owns minor-third and fourth color, upper string owns deadened offbeat scratches. After sixteen bars, Emi swaps the low and upper rhythmic roles without changing the harmonic center. Marcus leaves the drums unchanged, so the whole groove seems to rotate internally. Maya’s chorus uses compact unison vocals over major-7-to-dominant-9 FM harmony. A one-bar Body Break removes keys and bass, leaving drums, sanshin, and one bass-clarinet tongue-stop before the full groove returns.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Ferry-terminal service window marked 6, three narrow string lines drawn across a route map behind the glass, red stamp pad, aluminum frame, dim harbor lights outside. Sparse lyric fragments: “window six,” “three strings,” “change the lane,” “same fare, new step.”

## Track 3: Last Ferry Keeps the Swing

**Story & Context:** The closer runs at 98 BPM and begins with bass clarinet breath, rimshot, and isolated sanshin notes. Maya enters with the EP’s most intimate vocal, while Marcus keeps the drum grid almost mechanically stable. Emi uses fewer Skin Pickups and longer Slide Locks, sometimes beginning a whole tone below the destination and arriving only after the vocal line ends. In the final minute, FM keys and synth bass drop out. The sanshin, clap, and rimshot continue alone. Marcus removes the last programmed clap and leaves Emi to supply one final muted Clap Shadow. The EP ends on the short acoustic decay of the snakeskin resonator rather than a synth chord.

**Visual & Lyrics Prompt:** Nearly empty Naha ferry terminal after the final departure, timetable board dark except for one line, sanshin case resting beneath a cream service window, rainwater reflecting red and green lights on the floor. Sparse lyric fragments: “last ferry,” “keep the swing,” “no clap left,” “波だけ残る / only the waves remain.”

